From cc2b260ca554640f2d121502b8282c9f3f7375e6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GibaxLeGrand <48137851+GibaxLeGrand@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 02:47:12 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] StaticRecomp: hand the module Dolphin's exception word

For modules built with DOLRECOMP_EE_EXIT=pending (a switch of our local
copy of Piconet's DolRecomp fork, branch srnp/ee-pending): through the
module's staticrecomp_set_exceptions, generated code gets a pointer to
PowerPCState::Exceptions and, where a write sets MSR[EE], leaves for the
run loop only when an external interrupt is pending, which is the only
case where the run loop delivers one there. Before, every
OSRestoreInterrupts/OSEnableInterrupts left and unwound the native stack.
SRNP_EE_EXIT_ALWAYS=1 hands over nothing (the old exit).

Sonic Riders, demo race: fewer dispatches, no measurable speed change
(221.2-221.9 against 215.5-223.5 frames/s); deterministic; lockstep: the
same kinds of divergences.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
